From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 02:44:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] prime: an XBT datum gateway that discards 70-byte
 coinbasers is nta-unready (SOV-020)

The XBT datum lineages (StartOS 7491a50, iohzrd c031568, FTE, CONVOY) do not
truncate a coinbaser at a script over 64 bytes as OCEAN v0.4.1 :795 does; they
throw the whole coinbaser away ("Script length (70) is invalid. Using
default/empty"), build every job on that tip pool-only and cite coinbaser 0.
judge_nta only judged Split shares, so in a regtest lab both stayed unknown through
146 and 206 probes, were served after activation, and startos mined block 422
with a pool-only coinbase: bad-nta-count.

The session now remembers the last coinbaser it sent when it carried payees and
a 70-byte output (probe, or attestations after activation). A PoolOnly share on
a job with transactions at that height, first seen after it, is a strike; the
second makes the gateway nta-unready (CoinbaserDiscarded). One is not enough:
stock also publishes a pool-only section on the first notify of a height with
the split in hand (968440).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
